  "summary": "Simplify entertaining with these delicate <b>French herbed ricotta dumplings</b>, a refined make-ahead first course that highlights light cheese textures. Soft <b>whole milk ricotta</b> is blended with aged parmesan, farm egg yolks, and fragrant herbs like fresh chives and aromatic tarragon. Lightly bound with minimal flour, these tender dumplings yield a silky bite that melts effortlessly on the tongue. Shaping and chilling the dumplings in advance allows the structural protein framework to set firmly, making them ideal for prepping hours before a dinner party. Once gently poached in salted water, the dumplings rise gracefully to the surface, ready to be tossed in golden browned butter and lemon zest. This elegant dish provides a serene cooking experience for hosts who want high-end bistro quality without last-minute kitchen chaos. Serve sprinkled with extra parmesan and fresh herb leaves for an exquisite starter that tastes truly divine.",
